// S-693, S-611, S-596, §15.1, §18.1: the `pub use` of this version is E0200 (a failed name, the name stays
// silent where a `use` takes it: `use main.{g}`), but a path in a body of another module goes into the module
// through its items and its child modules alone, and `g` and `Mode` that `pub use` takes are neither: the last
// element and the middle of the path are E0302 (`main.g()`, `main.Mode.A`, `inner.g()`, `inner.Mode.A`).
// The items and the child modules that are there (`own`, `inner`, `h`) are the controls (`other.onsa`,
// `third.onsa`). `main/inner.onsa` has its own E0200. One error in each unit (§18.1).
pub use util.{g, Mode}                              //~ E0200 @1

pub fn own() -> I32 {
  1
}
